": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f341461b8902180882b2d832fa3f96b69e1eac9837e7d56b2ffb0adbca6e9f0b","event_uuid":"6705f2b0-3ea9-4c54-9051-835174705c6d","position":{"commit_sha":"3b26812244be65deff313f81fbf4874526fc769c","position":"1788986517782423001-6705f2b0-3ea9-4c54-9051-835174705c6d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f3bbbaf99f83c597dcfe7b00beb118264d6197c0cd0f55ecd56596f0438dab5e","event_uuid":"2546cf67-e75d-40a7-ab00-9ebeb19031d8","position":{"commit_sha":"3b26812244be65deff313f81fbf4874526fc769c","position":"1788986526085717001-2546cf67-e75d-40a7-ab00-9ebeb19031d8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788982178223188001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\nrebar MCP is configured globally per machine for all 3 harnesses, so every codex/claude/copilot session on the host gets it, and codex startup failed (2026-09-09) with a not-logged-in error when a GUI-launched process lacked MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX (valid PAT; 401 rendered as not-logged-in). Operator ruling: scope rebar MCP to this project via harness-native project mechanisms; claude+copilot consolidate onto one PAT var.\n\n## Plan (tracked-file half; machine-local half already applied)\n1. Add .mcp.json at repo root: rebar server entry, type http, url https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/, header Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI}. Read by Claude Code (project scope) AND Copilot CLI >=1.0.83 (workspace config; verified it loads .mcp.json first-found over .github/mcp.json and overrides user-level entries).\n2. Add [mcp_servers.rebar] to tracked .codex/config.toml: url https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/ + bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\" + startup_timeout_sec = 120 (carry the cold-start comment from the user-level config).\n3. Update infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md: document MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI (claude slot shared by Claude Code + Copilot CLI; codex keeps its own), the launchd-env publishing step (GUI launches do not source ~/.zshenv), and the project-scope files.\n4. If mcp-clients.local.example.json or docs/mcp-client-setup.md reference the old per-client global wiring, update the affected lines.\n\n\n## Established operator evidence / implementation notes\n- Do not re-derive: Copilot CLI 1.0.83 was empirically verified to load workspace `.mcp.json` first-found, ignore `.github/mcp.json` when present, and let workspace entries override user-level entries.\n- Do not re-derive: Claude Code reads `.mcp.json` as project scope and expands `${VAR}` in headers. The shared `.mcp.json` will therefore use the braced `${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI}` spelling and the post-merge verification must exercise a real Copilot CLI listing from `~/rebar` with the machine-local `launchctl` environment already published.\n- Do not re-derive: Codex reads tracked `.codex/config.toml`; the existing machine-local block already used `startup_timeout_sec = 120`, so the tracked project block carries the same key.\n- Operator ruling: Claude Code and Copilot CLI consolidate onto `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI`, a machine-local alias whose VALUE is the existing `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude` / `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE` slot; Codex keeps `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; no server-side SSM/keychain slot changes are in scope. The server authenticates the bearer value against the existing `claude` static-token digest record; there is no server-side `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` token_env record and the old copilot server slot remains populated but unused by the new project config.\n- Related consumer/doc surfaces to update or verify: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/README.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/claude/.mcp.json`, `examples/mcp-clients/copilot/mcp-config.json`, `examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml`, `mcp-clients.local.example.json`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py`, and `tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py`.\n- Machine-local cutover is expand/contract: first verify project-scope rebar resolves while global config still exists; then remove only global `rebar` entries; back-out is to restore the saved user-level rebar entry if project resolution regresses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.mcp.json` and `.codex/config.toml` define project-scope rebar MCP entries with env-var references only and URL `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/`; no secret values are committed; targeted tests prove the committed config resolves to accepted loopback bearers and rejects absent/wrong bearers.\n- [ ] Claude Code and Copilot CLI use `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` for the shared project-scope rebar entry, while Codex uses `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; no server-side SSM slot changes are made, and docs explain `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` is a local alias to the existing claude PAT value/server digest.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md` documents the CLI-PAT consolidation, launchd environment publishing for GUI-launched processes, and project-scope config files.\n- [ ] Existing setup docs/examples/tests that encode the old per-client global wiring are updated or explicitly verified as already current, including `docs/mcp-auth.md` if its per-client naming text is affected.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before push.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After merge, machine-local global rebar MCP entries are removed from Copilot, Claude, and Codex configs while keeping unrelated servers; first verify project-scope resolution while global exists, then verify project and non-project resolution after cutover, including actual rebar server listing/connection rather than config presence only, and record the host-local evidence in a ticket comment before close.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Run targeted config/documentation checks while implementing as needed.\n- Before Gerrit push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` from the fresh worktree.\n- Server-side auth proof: targeted tests model `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` as carrying the same value as the existing claude PAT record, so Copilot/Claude requests authenticate against the existing server-side `claude` digest without adding an SSM slot; Codex authenticates against the existing codex digest.\n- After merge and machine-local cutover, verify from `~/rebar`: `codex mcp get rebar`, `copilot mcp list`, and Claude project config resolution via `.mcp.json`; from a non-project directory (`~`), verify rebar is absent from global Codex/Copilot/Claude config surfaces.\n\n## File impact\n.mcp.json, .codex/config.toml, infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md, docs/mcp-client-setup.md (maybe), mcp-clients.local.example.json (maybe)","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".mcp.json","reason":"new project-scope MCP config for claude+copilot"},{"path":".codex/config.toml","reason":"add [mcp_servers.rebar] project entry"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md","reason":"document CLI PAT consolidation + launchd publishing"},{"path":"docs/mcp-client-setup.md","reason":"update client wiring docs if referenced"},{"path":"mcp-clients.local.example.json","reason":"update example if it references per-client global wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6705f2b0-3ea9-4c54-9051-835174705c6d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["mcp","config"],"ticket_id":"2240-b75a-81f0-4c30","ticket_type":"task","title":"Project-scope rebar MCP client config (codex/claude/copilot)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6dfd4a53-3886-4383-8b08-c52a36e3d8d0","aaf01019-3e91-40ae-8c3e-f67891a6b3f3","8cd50f41-967e-4896-93eb-e6c0aac397f0","238563ac-1dc3-4527-8c39-89a6ba4bcf51","ca3f64e6-823d-4a31-b405-b0c2c1214783","18b3bf91-4dad-4c8f-827c-c874108145c7","6705f2b0-3ea9-4c54-9051-835174705c6d","2546cf67-e75d-40a7-ab00-9ebeb19031d8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788994511341838001,"uuid":"843a279a-b8b9-426c-aecf-12d56c10feae"}